# CCTC

The [color=#5c6045]Creon-Centennial Trade Charter[/color] is a joint-venture shell company between Creon Industries and Centennial Armsworks, specifically created to pursue the fortune latent in the Colossus Sector. Officially given the sector development share by some unknown galactic rim government, the executives of the charter are keenly aware of the conflicting nature of the sector.

   Despite their official sector deed, the fact that the TSF, PDV, and innumerable well-armed adversaries inhabiting the sector all have their own claims makes their official ownership of the sector less impactful.

   While less physically powerful compared to the military forces of the [color=cyan]TSFMC[/color] and [color=tan]PDV[/color], the [color=#5c6045]Trade Charter[/color] wields something neither factions possess: Significant industrial production, which they are willing to lease out... for a price.

   While their industrial capability is the core of their strength, the [color=#5c6045]Trade Charter[/color] nonetheless has enough military power in the form of their leased [color=#ff5c4a]Centennial PMC[/color] mercenaries, who wield the most advanced technology available to them.
   The [color=#5c6045]Trade Charter[/color] is ultimately in the region for one goal:

  > [bold][color=red]Make as much money as humanly possible.[/bold][/color]


# Hierarchy (I-VI)

   Of course, a company like that of the [color=#5c6045]Creon-Centennial Trade Charter[/color] has different levels of employment.

(I)   [color=gold]Oligarch[/color] is the [bold]highest ranking[/bold] within the [color=#5c6045]Trade Charter[/color] and is one of the managers of the shell company. They have the final say in any matter regarding operations when they deign to mettle in the affairs of their lower-networth employees. While they technically command the operations in the sector, they more often sit in the station and benefit from the work of their underlings and let others do the bulk of the work.

(II)   [color=yellow]Shareholders[/color] are the [bold]second highest[/bold] level [color=#5c6045]Trade Charter[/color] members, and are behave similarly to nobles from other galactic empires, riding on the wealth of the company. Despite their wealth, they ultimately answer to executive board officials such as the resident oligarchs, and seek to please them at all costs in order to benefit from a shred of their amassed wealth.

(III-1)   Centennial [color=#0c977c]Marshalls[/color] command station operations, ensuring everything is running smoothly in lieu of their richer employers. They also serve as commanders of the Centennial PMC hired for protection, and are often on the front-lines when enforcement of charter interests is needed.

(III-2)  [color=lightblue]Claims Managers[/color] manage Creon-Centennial's medical branch, ensuring proper medical aid is given to properly paying customers. Usually drive a tough bargain, with those failing to meet their egregious terms meeting the local Centennial PMC.

(IV)   Centennial [color=#ff5c4a]Judges[/color] function as hired Centennial PMC goons, equipped with the latest in Centennial-provided armament and tasked with doing whatever their employers require. Often this comes in the form of enforcing charter interests, or just moving stuff around. Dealing with frustrated customers in a "cordial" manner is just part of the job.

(V)   Charter [color=5c6045]Service Techs[/color] are specialists employed by the trade charter to handle the dirty work of the company's industrial operations. They are tasked with repairing, upgrading, designing and operating charter industry, securing contracts, and ensuring everything runs smoothly on the factory floor.

(VI)   Charter [color=lightblue]Medics[/color] are medical doctors employed by the trade charter to take up the lucrative task of saving anybody who meets their end at the hand of the sector's many dangers, making sure their customers are especially "generous."

# S.O.P (Standard Operating Procedure)

  [color=#5c6045]Creon-Centennial Trade Charter[/color], while boasting some level of military power due to the conflict in the sector, is ultimately present to establish lucrative industry and please upper management.
  As such, all members of the Charter are expected to follow the below guidelines:

  > Maintain plausible deniability for any tragedies that happen in-sector

  > Maintain positive reputation for the Charter (i.e Avoid making enemies in-sector)

  > Do not displease shareholders through uneccessary warfare
